<p>Those of you who watch and enjoy unique movies — do you think Blu-ray players are still worth it? How much of your collection, assuming you have one, is on Blu-ray?</p>
<p>The story so far:</p>
<p>Earlier this year, I watched <a href="https://taonaw.com/2026/02/09/iron-lung.html">Iron Lung</a> with Nat and RKWB. I enjoyed myself. I think it was well made, especially considering how it was made and by whom, which makes the whole project interesting in terms of filmmaking.</p>
<p>Anywho, Markiplier, the guy behind the movie, is now distributing it on DVD and Blu-ray. Those contain special behind-the-scenes footage of how challenging (apparently) it is to make Blu-ray releases nowadays. This movie is a collectible item (at least for Nat), which might make it worth owning a Blu-ray player. Or not. For one movie&hellip;? Well, that&rsquo;s the question.</p>
<p>It seems like there&rsquo;s a pattern here. First, I got a CD-ROM drive three and a half years ago (which I still have) after going to a <a href="https://taonaw.com/2023/05/24/a-cult-movie.html">specialty movie store in Brooklyn</a>. Then we got our <a href="https://taonaw.com/2025/04/26/im-so-used-to-watch.html">Sony TV</a>. Is this the next step…?</p>
